@startuml start-from-awaiting-merge-decision
' cumin-works - an implementation issue that starts from the branch of a pull request
' that waits for the merge decision (IMPL-008, MERGE-013).
' Issue #1 is the blocker. Issue #2 is blocked by #1 and starts from the branch of #1.
' Render: run scripts/render-diagrams.sh at the root of the repository.

hide footbox

actor "Assignee" as Assignee
participant "cumin" as Cumin
participant "Implementer\n(issue #2)" as Impl
participant "main" as Main
participant "branch of #1" as B1
participant "branch of #2" as B2

== issue #1 waits for the merge decision ==

note over Main, B1 : pull request of #1: base main,\nissue #1 is awaiting-merge-decision
Cumin -> Cumin : issue #2 is ready, and its only open blocker\nissue #1 is awaiting-merge-decision (IMPL-008.1)
Cumin -> Impl : request the implementation,\nstarting from the branch of #1 (IMPL-008.2)
B1 -> B2 : branch off
Impl -> B2 : commit and push
Impl -> B2 : open a pull request with base: branch of #1
note over B1, B2 : the diff shows only the change of #2.\nNew commits on the branch of #1 are not followed (IMPL-008.3)

... required checks and review of #2 ...

Cumin -> Cumin : the Reviewer approved #2, but its base is not main\n→ #2 is awaiting-blocker-merge (MERGE-013)

== the Assignee merges #1 ==

Assignee -> Cumin : approve the pull request of #1
Cumin -> Main : merge the pull request of #1
note over Main, B2 : GitHub deletes the branch of #1\nand changes the base of #2 to main
Cumin -> Impl : take in the main branch and check again\nagainst the merged #1 (IMPL-008.4)\n→ #2 is implementing
Main -> B2 : merge commit of main

... required checks, review, and merge decision of #2 ...

Cumin -> Main : merge the pull request of #2

== if the pull request of #1 is closed without a merge ==

Cumin -> Cumin : stop #2\n→ #2 is awaiting-decision (IMPL-008.5)

@enduml
